{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Description replaced (re-based on `origin/main` 403719c01ce). What changed and why:\n\n**1. AC1 was unsatisfiable; the obvious fix was also wrong.**\n\nThe old AC1 grep (`_ALIASES\\b|...`) returns **30 hits across 18 files** on an untouched tree, of which only **9** are in scope. `_ALIASES\\b` binds only the right edge, so it also matches `_HIDDEN_ALIASES` (11), `_REMOVED_SIMPLE_CLI_ALIASES`, `_EDIT_FLAG_ALIASES`, `_DEPRECATED_PROVIDER_ALIASES`, `_ARCH_ALIASES`, `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`. The story could be implemented perfectly and AC1 would still fail on a pandoc architecture map.\n\nThree `tests/fixtures/**` corpora (`cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json:29`, `dc_wiki_corpus/prose.json:109`, `dc_wiki_corpus/table.json:13`) embed captured prose quoting `_map_legacy_env` and `_HIDDEN_ALIASES`. That corpus is frozen and must never be edited, so left-edge binding alone is still not enough — the AC also needs `':(exclude)tests/fixtures'`.\n\n**The non-obvious part:** my first corrected regex was `-nE '(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])(...)\\b'`. Run verbatim it returns **zero hits on an unmodified tree** — `git grep -E` silently ignores `\\b`. That AC would have passed vacuously, certifying a deletion that never happened. This is the same defect class as a hardcoded count: a check that cannot fail is not a check.\n\nVerified empirically, on `origin/main`:\n\n| form | result |\n|---|---|\n| `-E` with `\\b` | **0 hits — broken** |\n| `-E` with `([^A-Za-z0-9_]\\|$)` both sides | 9 hits ✓ |\n| BRE `\\(^\\|[^A-Za-z0-9_]\\)...\\b` | 9 hits ✓ |\n| `-P` with lookbehind | works, but needs git built with PCRE |\n\nAC1 now uses the ERE form (portable, no PCRE dependency), carries the expected pre-state (**exactly 9**) so the AC is falsifiable, and explicitly warns against \"simplifying\" it back to `\\b`.\n\n**2. The story is partially superseded.** `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` and `_map_legacy_env` exist nowhere in `src`. They were deleted by **`e096a33d3b7` \"Delete the empty legacy env alias table\", `rebar-ticket: 25a4-1ab3-3558-4cd4`** — a sibling in this epic that landed after this plan was written. `_config_sources.py` is now **317 lines**, so the cited `:330-339`, `:342-352` and `:357-363` are all past EOF. That module moved to Out of scope.\n\n**3. One citation would have broken this story's own AC3.** The old plan said to delete `config.py:9,45,56` and `:382-385`. `config.py` (624 lines) has **exactly one** alias reference, at `:9`. `:45` is `env_overrides,`, `:56` is `resolve_acli_call_timeout`, and `:382-385` is the `raise_or_warn_env`/tombstone machinery the plan explicitly keeps — and that AC3 depends on. Following the old text literally would have deleted the code AC3 tests. The Approach now flags `:382-385` as KEEP, and AC3 repeats it.\n\n**4. ~11 further line drifts** corrected, including the `_deprecations.py` registry rows: the old cites `:209-217` and `:226-241` point at the functions that *consume* the rows, not the rows (`:135-176`).\n\n**Re-verified as sound — not drift, do not \"fix\" these:** `tombstones()` returns **19 rows = 6 error + 13 warn**, all `removed_in=\"v1.0.0\"`, and the 6 named error rows match exactly. `coerce_sparse` measures **exactly 15** against `max-complexity = 15`, which is what forces the alias-loop removal (−3) and the `[llm]` branch (+1) to land together. `gen_config_reference.py:224-233` and `docs/api-stability.md:27` are exact. `_env_aliases()` returns `{}` (the sole `REGISTRY` row is `cfg`-kind), so the \"no output change\" claim holds — and `gen_env_registry.py:19` already cites `REGISTRY`, so half that edit is already done.\n\nScope, Testing and the other four ACs are unchanged in substance."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793424003909649951,"uuid":"8f15c701-8284-41b6-a614-327eb80ef321"}